```sql
--Description / Thinking process:
-- Our objective is two-fold:
--   1) Determine which Utah ZIP code(s) have the FEWEST FDIC-insured bank
--      branch locations (using FDA.FDIC_BANKS.LOCATIONS).
--   2) Retrieve the 2017 American Community Survey (ACS) employment-rate for
--      the population aged 16+ for those ZIP codes.
--
-- The only way to accomplish step 2 is if an ACS table containing ZIP-level
-- 2017 employment-rate data exists in a schema we can access.  Suppose such a
-- table were loaded into FDA.CENSUS_UTILITY as
--       ACS_2017_ZIP_EMPLOYMENT
-- with at least the columns:
--       "zip_code"                – five-digit ZIP
--       "employment_rate_16_plus" – employment-population ratio, age ≥16
--
-- The query below therefore:
--   • Counts branch locations per ZIP for Utah (state = 'UT').
--   • Filters to the ZIP code(s) whose count equals the statewide minimum.
--   • Joins those ZIP(s) to the hypothetical ACS table to obtain the
--     employment-rate figure.
-- If the ACS table is not present, the query will error; in that case step 2
-- cannot be completed with the current data catalog.
WITH fewest_zip AS (                       /* ZIP(s) having the fewest FDIC branches */
    SELECT  "zip_code"
    FROM   (SELECT "zip_code",
                   COUNT(*) AS loc_cnt
            FROM   FDA.FDIC_BANKS.LOCATIONS
            WHERE  "state" = 'UT'
            GROUP  BY "zip_code") z
    QUALIFY loc_cnt = MIN(loc_cnt) OVER () /* keep only minimum-count ZIP(s) */
)
SELECT a."zip_code",
       a."employment_rate_16_plus"
FROM   FDA.CENSUS_UTILITY.ACS_2017_ZIP_EMPLOYMENT a   /* hypothetical ACS table */
JOIN   fewest_zip f
  ON   a."zip_code" = f."zip_code";
```
